{"id": "EUVD-2026-96901", "enisaUuid": "42232744-c045-3968-8c7d-8d6699583e24", "description": "Miniflux 2.3.0 through 2.3.3 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows authenticated users to reach internal addresses by setting a feed's proxy_url. Attackers can point proxy_url at loopback or internal hosts, bypassing FETCHER_ALLOW_PRIVATE_NETWORKS checks to probe internal ports and send proxy-style requests to internal services.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T12:19:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T13:24:24", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind03/miniflux-feed-proxy-url-private-network-bypass", "https://github.com/miniflux/v2/blob/c4d54f87a81b30aa173fddf05d7ff83ae7da5796/internal/reader/fetcher/request_builder.go#L155-L220", "https://github.com/miniflux/v2/blob/c4d54f87a81b30aa173fddf05d7ff83ae7da5796/internal/urllib/url.go#L64-L72", "https://github.com/miniflux/v2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/miniflux-2.3.0-through-2.3.3-ssrf-via-per-feed-proxy-url"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108735", "GHSA-f5cv-wgfv-h2x2"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2e2e74f7-b6f4-336d-b92c-5c067d7a2d88", "product": {"name": "miniflux", "vendor": {"name": "miniflux"}}, "product_version": "2.3.0 \u22642.3.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b02680f6-fb49-39ea-ab8d-b334030c2286", "vendor": {"name": "miniflux"}}], "isExploited": false}